From c8861d8968cc9da016f5c55385956a2757068e0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 10:22:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 85/90] usb: dwc3: Require MPS-aligned OUT buffers

An OUT request whose length is not a multiple of the maximum packet size
gets an extra TRB pointing at a shared bounce buffer, so that a final
full packet from the host has somewhere to land. Bytes the host sends
past the end of the request land in that buffer and are dropped without
the function driver ever hearing about it, silently desynchronising a
byte stream.

Set quirk_ep_out_aligned_size so the framework rounds OUT buffers up to
the maximum packet size and the overflow cannot happen.
Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
index 88792b22efc1..d92f91eac235 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
@@ -4815,6 +4815,16 @@ int dwc3_gadget_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 				dwc->revision);
 
 	dwc->gadget->max_speed		= dwc->maximum_speed;
+
+	/*
+	 * An OUT request that is not a multiple of the maximum packet size gets
+	 * an extra TRB pointing at a shared bounce buffer, so that a final full
+	 * packet from the host has somewhere to land. Anything the host sends
+	 * past the end of the request ends up in that buffer and is discarded -
+	 * see dwc3_gadget_ep_reclaim_completed_trb(). Tell the gadget framework
+	 * to round OUT buffers up instead, so the situation cannot arise.
+	 */
+	dwc->gadget->quirk_ep_out_aligned_size = true;
 	dwc->gadget->max_ssp_rate	= dwc->max_ssp_rate;
 
 	/*
